Subject: [PATCH] dvd_input: read unencrypted discs only, never load a decryption library (libdvdread 7.x)

Without libdvdcss at build time the original code tries dlopen("libdvdcss.so.2") at run time and, if a
copy is present on the system, uses it to decrypt CSS protected discs. The image must never
decrypt, so the run time loading and the functions using it are removed; sectors are read
directly (discs without protection). Linking against the library at build time is not used
(PACKAGECONFIG without libdvdcss). Port of the libdvdread 6.1.3 patch to 7.1.1.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [distribution policy]
